1453..1526 Comment "/// The winding number into the native integers, a fold that rests on the"
1527..1584 Comment "/// native model\'s laws. At `Loop(Unloop(x))` it computes"
1585..1656 Comment "/// `turn(unturn(native_wind(x)))`, which conversion does not reduce to"
1657..1733 Comment "/// `native_wind(x)` on a variable; the law `turnUnturn` states exactly that"
1734..1810 Comment "/// path, so `respects` names it for the first rule and `unturnTurn` for the"
1811..1885 Comment "/// second. The loop arms call the model\'s operations rather than spelling"
1886..1964 Comment "/// `n + 1`, so each side the rule relates is the law\'s own endpoint. The fold"
1965..2007 Comment "/// checks and owes what its two laws owe."
